"""Learning paths: six disciplines x platforms x three levels (Crawl, Walk, Run).

How it fits together
- CONCEPTS: one job (the concept) and the product that does it on each platform (the physical thing).
  Topics name concepts, so a page for "Data Engineering on AWS" shows AWS products and the same
  page for GCP shows GCP products. Learn the concept once; the product is a binding.
- PROJECTS: GitHub projects people build at each level. `site` links to an existing /projects/ page;
  status "proposed" means nobody leads it yet.
- DISCIPLINES: who it is for, the platforms it supports, and the three levels.

To add a platform name, edit CONCEPTS. To add a project, add it to PROJECTS and list its id in a level.
"""

